| ROUTER | Model Resource Manager — tier selection (virtual, in model-orchestration) |

## System prompts (shared/agent-prompts.ts)

```typescript
export const AGENT_SYSTEM_PROMPTS: Record<string, string> = {
  DESK: "You are DESK...",
  CODE: "You are CODE...",
  // 109/109 coverage required
};
```

**Rule:** Adding agent to AGENTS[] requires matching prompt key (uppercase name).

## Agent details (shared/agent-details.ts)

Extended profiles: capabilities, tools, model recommendations, useCases.
Used by AgentDetail page and `/api/agents/:name`.

## Intent routing flow

```
User message
  → DESK analyzes intent (server/router/classifier.ts)
    → suggests 1-N specialist agents
      → POST /api/router/execute or /api/chat with agent param
```

Classifier types in `shared/__tests__/openapi-classifier.test.ts`.

## Organization Blueprint V1 (shared/organization.ts)

Maps existing 109 agents into **8 AI Companies** without creating new agents:

| Company ID | Name |
|------------|------|
| software | Nirva Software Company |
| commerce | Commerce Company |
| media | Media Company |
| service | Service Company |
| business-support | Business Support |
| knowledge | Knowledge System |
| investment-legal | Investment & Legal |

Each company has `departments[]` → `agents[]` with blueprintRole, skills, modelTier, model.

API: `GET /api/organization` returns full tree.
Stats: `getOrganizationStats()` — company count, department count, unique agents.

## Permissions (shared/permissions.ts)

Role-based access matrix for multi-tenant features.
API: `GET /api/permissions`

## Marketplace integration

Agents can export/import skills via `/api/marketplace/export/:agentName`.
Marketplace categories in `shared/marketplace.ts`.

